instruction:
Quick, precise follow-up edit in the Go repo at /gin (github.com/gin-gonic/gin). Do NOT use the internet. Do NOT touch any *_test.go file. Do NOT touch errors.go, gin.go, response_writer.go, tree.go. Only edit /gin/context.go.

Current state of func (c *Context) NegotiateFormat in /gin/context.go (around line 1120) contains this loop:

			i := 0
			for ; i < len(accepted); i++ {
				// The offer may be shorter than the accepted format, in which case
				// it cannot match: stop comparing instead of indexing out of range.
				if i >= len(offer) {
					break
				}
				if accepted[i] == '*' || offer[i] == '*' {
					return offer
				}
				if accepted[i] != offer[i] {
					break
				}
			}
			// Only an exact (or wildcard) match counts: a format that is merely a
			// prefix of the other one is not acceptable.
			if i == len(accepted) && i == len(offer) {
				return offer
			}

Replace it with the MINIMAL fix that only prevents the out-of-range panic and otherwise preserves the original behaviour exactly (an accepted format that is a prefix of the offer still matches, i.e. the final check stays `if i == len(accepted) { return offer }`):

			i := 0
			for ; i < len(accepted) && i < len(offer); i++ {
				if accepted[i] == '*' || offer[i] == '*' {
					return offer
				}
				if accepted[i] != offer[i] {
					break
				}
			}
			if i == len(accepted) {
				return offer
			}

Do not change anything else in the file (the FileAttachment hunk added by another agent must stay as it is).

Then verify quickly:
1. `cd /gin && gofmt -l context.go` (must be empty) and `go build ./...`.
2. `cd /gin && GOFLAGS=-mod=mod GOPROXY=off GOSUMDB=off go test -count=1 ./...` — must be fully green (all packages ok, no failures).
3. Write a temporary test OUTSIDE the repo (e.g. /tmp/negfix with a go.mod containing `require github.com/gin-gonic/gin v0.0.0` and `replace github.com/gin-gonic/gin => /gin`) or a scratch _test.go inside /gin that you DELETE afterwards, checking: Accept "image/tiff-fx" with c.NegotiateFormat("image/tiff") returns "" and does not panic; Accept "image/tiff" with c.NegotiateFormat("image/tiff-fx") returns "image/tiff-fx" (prefix behaviour preserved); Accept "text/html,application/xhtml+xml,application/xml;q=0.9;q=0.8" with (MIMEJSON, MIMEXML) returns MIMEXML and with (MIMEXML, MIMEHTML) returns MIMEHTML and (MIMEJSON) returns ""; wildcard cases: Accept "*/*" with "text/*" returns "text/*"; Accept "text/*" with MIMEHTML returns MIMEHTML and with MIMEJSON returns "".
4. `git -C /gin status --untracked-files=all` — report it; there must be no untracked scratch files left in /gin.

Report concisely: the exact diff you applied, the test-suite result, the outcome of each check above, and confirm no scratch files remain.
